 "real_look_note": "golden_hour preset (kit/light_presets.py), held for the whole film; the key values are also written out here (equal to the preset). No blueprint/x-ray graphics, default label cards. Ground colour: a yellow-orange sun (#FFB462, sun glow #FFBE72), a blue sky fill (#8DB0D4, not violet) and warm-stone piazza/paving albedo (real_palette) keep the grey paving from reading pink-purple. sun_glow 0.6 / sun_glow_width 0.3 keep the into-sun shots (27-36 s) from washing the sky peach. sun_keys dims the key sun to 10 % for the relieving-arch diagram (ramp 20.3-21.8 s during the orbit, back to 100 % on the hard cut at 27.0 s) so the front-lit drum stays darker than the orange arches / gold force lines.",
 "grade_note": "overlay.py grade = the golden_hour preset grade (vignette, bottom darkening, S-curve, split tone) plus 'off' spans. hue_fix band 1 pulls low-saturation pink/salmon/mauve (296-34 deg, soft 40) to warm stone 32 deg; band 2 gently pulls lilac (228-298 deg, soft 35, k 0.6) toward blue 222 deg. The two bands meet only across wide soft edges: a hard split between them folds smooth gradients (sun glow, palazzi roofs) into a magenta/green seam. shadow_cool adds a little blue to near-neutral shadows. hue_fix and shadow_cool are off in the scan interior (12.375-15.0 s, hard cuts at both ends) so the photo scan keeps its approved colours.",
